+PRI showIdleFrameSet() : nShownPosts | pSet1, pSet2, pShown, pIdle, setLongs, bAccepted
+' Exercise display.showFrameSet() on a set the caller built: copy the frame set on display into
+' the other set (so the picture does not change) and post it with showFrameSet(); then offer the
+' screen buffer's address, which must be refused. Every commit converts into the set not on
+' display, so after an odd number of commits set 1 is on display (the first commit converts into
+' set 1). The take check counts the accepted post as one more take; posting the wrong set would
+' repost the set on display, which no take marks, so the take check would FAIL.
+'
+' @returns nShownPosts - frame sets posted by showFrameSet() (1 when it accepted the idle set)
+
+' Local Variables:
+' @local pSet1 - hub address of the adapter's frame set 1
+' @local pSet2 - hub address of the adapter's frame set 2
+' @local pShown - the set on display
+' @local pIdle - the set not on display
+' @local setLongs - longs in one frame set
+' @local bAccepted - what showFrameSet() answered
+
+  nShownPosts := 0
+  waitms(TAKE_SETTLE_MS)                                        ' the last commit's post is taken
+  pSet1 := hub75Bffrs.pwmFrame1BufferAddress(chainIndex)
+  pSet2 := hub75Bffrs.pwmFrame2BufferAddress(chainIndex)
+  pShown := pSet2
+  pIdle := pSet1
+  if commitsPosted() // ODD_DIVISOR == 1
+    pShown := pSet1
+    pIdle := pSet2
+  setLongs := hub75Bffrs.pwmFrameSizeInLongs(chainIndex) * hub75Bffrs.pwmFrameCount(chainIndex)
+  longmove(pIdle, pShown, setLongs)
+  bAccepted := display.showFrameSet(pIdle)
+  if bAccepted == TRUE
+    nShownPosts := 1
+    debug("RATES: PASS: showFrameSet() accepted the set not on display (", uhex_long_(pIdle), "); the take check counts its take")
+  else
+    debug("RATES: FAIL: showFrameSet() refused the set not on display (", uhex_long_(pIdle), ")")
+  bAccepted := display.showFrameSet(hub75Bffrs.displayBufferAddress(chainIndex))
+  if bAccepted == FALSE
+    debug("RATES: PASS: showFrameSet() refused the screen buffer's address (its message is the line above)")
+  else
+    nShownPosts++
+    debug("RATES: FAIL: showFrameSet() accepted the screen buffer's address")
+
 PRI drawPhase(phaseIdx) | drawStart, commitStart
 ' Draw one phase into the screen buffer and commit it, timing each step.
 '
